   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/VectorBundle/Basic.lean:193 `theorem linearEquivAt_apply ... : e.linearEquivAt R b hb v = (e \u27e8b, v\u27e9).2 := rfl` and :198 `theorem linearEquivAt_symm_apply ... : (e.linearEquivAt R b hb).symm v = e.symm b v := rfl`, both `@[simp]`. After `Module.Basis.map_repr`/`map_apply` and `LinearEquiv.symm_symm` the goal is `(e_\u03b2.linearEquivAt \ud835\udd5c x h\u03b2) ((e_\u03b1.linearEquivAt \ud835\udd5c x h\u03b1).symm (b j)) = tangentCoordChange I \u03b1 \u03b2 x (b j)`, which these two rewrite to the `((e_\u03b2) \u27e8x, e_\u03b1.symm x (b j)\u27e9).2 = ...` form of `hread` (the same form the author obtains at lines 436-439 via `continuousLinearMapAt_apply_of_mem`/`symmL_apply`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Tangent.lean",
   "fix": "Replace `symm; rw [LinearEquiv.symm_symm]; change ...; exact hread` with explicit rewrites, e.g. `rw [Bundle.Trivialization.linearEquivAt_apply, Bundle.Trivialization.linearEquivAt_symm_apply]; exact hread.symm` (or add both, plus `LinearEquiv.symm_symm`, to the `simp only` at line 430 and close with `exact hread.symm`), and drop the comment.",
